; A REPOSITORY-LEVEL integration test. It reads Makefile, tools/target-matrix.sh
; and tools/dev/dump-target-config.sh, all of which are OUTSIDE the asm/ dune
; workspace, so it cannot be a runtest rule: reaching them through ../ or an
; absolute path would make a sandboxed action depend on undeclared inputs, which
; is worse than not sandboxing at all.
;
; It is therefore built here and RUN BY MAKE (tools-integration), with the
; repository root passed as argv - so the root a command operated on is visible
; in the command line rather than inferred, and %{workspace_root} (which is
; asm/, not the repository root) never enters.

(executables
 (names repo_tests)
 (modes byte native)
 (libraries compcert_tools err_trace bos fpath unix))
